cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "sus-grad-correlation: suspiciousness and gradient correlation experiments for neural networks"
abstract: >-
  Code and reproduction container for two experiments asking whether the neurons
  that spectrum-based fault localisation (SBFL) calls suspicious are the same
  neurons that carry a large loss gradient. Experiment 1 measures the
  correlation across 100 randomly initialised copies of each model at fixed
  epochs; experiment 2 follows one model's values across 200 epochs of training.
type: software
